      "tasks": [
        "Launch only owned loopback processes against fresh synthetic state; record tools/artifacts/environment and exact owned PID start times.",
        "Implement bounded readiness, timeout, cancellation and teardown; preserve every failed setup/run and reject blank/intermediate screenshots.",
        "Keep each comparator/runtime operation in its own module; split before exceeding the shared review budget.",
        "Re-review RR15: complete its bounded repair and consuming-caller verification before acceptance; original scope remains required."
      ],
      "verification": [
        "Inject divergent inputs/results and prove failure; retain raw observations and human-readable diffs.",
        "Exercise an actual existing native and Rust fixture through the public harness interface; no mocked runtime equivalence."
      ],
      "commit_plan": [
        "Freeze the concrete source contracts and matched fixtures; keep oracle captures separate from expectations.",
        "Implement one behavior family with meaningful regression and actual caller integration.",
        "Record exact execution inputs, original failures, passing receipts and independent disposition."
      ],
      "budget": "Aim <=400 changed handwritten production lines and <=900 authored lines including tests. Split by named operation/widget before execution if larger; generated tables and evidence are separate commits.",
